(5, 'In Arabic, which vowel point can modify a consonant to create a long vowel sound?', 'Fathah (ـَ)', 'Kasrah (ـِ)', 'Dammah (ـُ)', 'Sukun (ـْ)', 'C'),
(6, 'Which vowel point is used to represent a short \"a\" sound in Arabic words?', 'Fathah (ـَ)', 'Kasrah (ـِ)', 'Dammah (ـُ)', 'Shaddah (ـّ)', 'A'),
(7, 'How many vowel points, including \"Fathah,\" are there in Arabic script?', '3', '29', '18', '4', 'C'),
(8, 'What does the \"Fathah\" vowel point indicate when added to a consonant in Arabic?', 'An \"a\" sound', 'An \"i\" sound', 'An \"u\" sound', 'No sound', 'A'),
(9, 'What type of sound does the \"Fathah\" vowel point represent in Arabic?', 'A short \"i\" sound', 'A long \"a\" sound', 'A short \"u\" sound', 'A long \"i\" sound', 'B'),
(10, 'Which vowel point appears as a dot above a letter in Arabic script?', 'Kasrah (ـِ)', 'Dammah (ـُ)', 'Fathah (ـَ)', 'Shaddah (ـّ)', 'C'),
