(207, 'Argues that the state of nature was rampant with conflict and violence:', 'Thomas Hobbes', 'Alexander the Great', 'Friedrich Engels', 'John Locke', 'A'),
(208, 'Peace is an earthly expression of God\'s Kingdom that is yet uncorrupted. This is the belief of:', 'Sociologists', 'Politicians', 'Philosophers', 'Theologians', 'C'),
(209, 'The earth was initially created as a peaceful environment but was later corrupted by Man\'s greed. This is the position of:', 'John Locke', 'Karl Marx', 'Jean Rousseau', 'Hegel', 'C'),
(210, 'According to the instrumentalist, the central function of both the social and political systems is to create:', 'Love', 'Development', 'Peace', 'Harmony', 'C'),
(211, 'The instrumentalist in peace study is also known as:', 'The Progressive', 'The Successful', 'The Functionalist', 'The Pioneers', 'C'),
(212, 'The problem of the instrumentalist is that they failed to understand that peace is:', 'Universal', 'an end in itself', 'Survival', 'Necessary', 'B'),
(213, 'Sees justice as the basis of peaceful social existence:', 'Aristotle', 'Socrates', 'Plato', 'Archimedes', 'C'),
(214, 'There can never be peace without:', 'Love', 'Social Harmony', 'Justice', 'Transparency', 'B'),
(215, 'Refers to a condition of social harmony in which there is no conflict:', 'Sociologists', 'Physiocrats', 'Mercantilist', 'Socialized', 'A'),
(216, 'Opines that to understand the society, we have to look at the process of production and distribution of material resources in the society:', 'Trevor Ropper', 'Ilegal Adams', 'Smith', 'Karl Marx', 'D'),
(217, 'Is a tradition of social analysis that sees society as a mosaic of functions and structures that perform them:', 'Structuralist and Functionalist', 'Instrumentalist', 'Atheist', 'Politician', 'A'),
(218, 'The proponent of the Marxist ideology is from which country:', 'England', 'France', 'Germany', 'Spain', 'C'),
(219, 'Peace has many definitions given to it, and the following are the definitions except:', 'Sociological', 'Philosophical', 'Political', 'Religious', 'D'),
(220, 'Peace is a prerequisite in human society because without it, there will be no:', 'Religion', 'Market', 'Development', 'Educational', 'C'),
(221, 'In peace study, institutionalization means that political structures:', 'Are created', 'Are observed', 'Acquired value and stability', 'Are repeated', 'C'),
(222, 'According to ___________, peace is a political condition that makes justice possible:', 'University of Peace', 'University on Peace', 'University for Peace', 'University with Peace', 'C');
INSERT INTO `gst_202` (`id`, `question`, `option_a`, `option_b`, `option_c`, `option_d`, `answer`) VALUES
(223, '________________ view sees peace as a contractual fact:', 'Sociological', 'Political', 'Philosophical', 'Theological View', 'B'),
(224, '________________ sees peace as a condition in which all men are born free and exist as gentle savages:', 'John Don', 'Jean Rousseau', 'Thomas Hobbes', 'Hegel', 'B'),
(225, 'The prevalence of a breach of peace in Nigeria could be linked to:', 'Poverty', 'Religion', 'Education', 'Illiteracy', 'A'),
(226, 'To create peace, politics must be mediated by stable structures and secular culture. This is ________________ view:', 'Sociological', 'Political', 'Philosophical', 'Economic', 'B'),
(227, '__________________ is the main reason for the creation of the United Nations organization:', 'WWII', 'Economic growth', 'Peace', 'Love for humanity', 'C'),
(228, 'Negotiation is one of the effective ways for:', 'Love', 'Peace', 'Resolution', 'Agreement', 'B'),
(229, 'The current IPOB uprising is an example of the absence of:', 'Sociological peace', 'Political peace', 'Philosophical peace', 'Economical peace', 'B'),
(230, 'For conflict to be resolved, there must be a:', 'Argument', 'Process', 'Discussion', 'Forgiveness', 'B'),
(231, 'The idea of a \'beloved society\' was propounded by:', 'Mehetna', 'Ghaudi', 'Martin Lurther King', 'Karl Marx', 'C'),
(232, 'The experience of the WWII showed that without peace, the world is:', 'A prosperous place', 'A dangerous place', 'An industrial place', 'A progression place', 'B'),
(233, 'One of the following is a good ingredient for the peace process:', 'Impatience', 'Courage', 'Argument', 'Prejudice', 'B'),
(234, 'The structural conflict theory is represented by the following scholars except:', 'Ross Rose', 'V.I. Lenin', 'Marx', 'B', NULL),
(235, 'Structuralists maintain that conflicts occur because of:', 'Injustice', 'Selfishness', 'Aggression', 'Corruption', 'A'),
(236, 'The main argument of structural conflict theory is that societies are:', 'Underdeveloped', 'Structured and arranged', 'Structured and Organized', 'Organized and developed', 'C'),
(237, 'Liberal Structuralists such as ________ propounded the theory of negative peace and positive peace:', 'Walter Rodney', 'Johan Galtung', 'Samir Amin', 'Andre Frank', 'B'),
(238, '_______ are factors that are responsible for the emergence of internal conflict except:', 'Overpopulation', 'Demographics', 'Environmental', 'Economic', 'A'),
(239, 'The following are components of realist theory except:', 'Perspective realism', 'Prescriptive realism', 'Explanatory realism', 'Descriptive realism', 'A'),
(240, '_______ realism shows that there are genetic effects which push man to behave negatively:', 'Perspective realism', 'Prescriptive realism', 'Explanatory realism', 'Descriptive realism', 'C'),
(241, '_________ described the destructive tendencies in human beings as dialectical struggle:', 'Sigmund Freud', 'Thomas Hobbes', 'Malthus', 'Augustine', 'A'),
(242, 'The Frustration aggression theory was developed in the year:', '1929', '1937', '1949', '1939', 'D'),
(243, '_________ theory of conflict has given rise to what may be referred to as the innate theory:', 'Realist', 'Karl Marx', 'Rodney\'s', 'Biological', 'D'),
(244, 'Relational theory of conflict attempts to provide an explanation for violent conflicts by explaining:', 'Agnatic relationship', 'Biological relationship', 'Economic relationship', 'System relationship', 'C'),
(245, 'The exploitation of the proletariat and lower classes under capitalism creates ________:', 'Peace', 'Conflict', 'Understanding', 'War', 'B'),
(246, 'Which of the following sees conflict as an arena of conflict:', 'Perspective realism', 'Descriptive realism', 'Prescriptive realism', 'Explanatory realism', 'B'),
(247, 'Walt argues that conflict has its roots in forces that are inherent in ________:', 'Human nature', 'Birth', 'Anger', 'Injustice', 'A'),
(248, 'The realists share similar principles with the following except:', 'Biological theory', 'Physiological theory', 'Theological theory', 'Relational theory', 'D'),
(249, 'Collier pointed out that some people commonly referred to as _______ benefit from chaos:', 'Social entrepreneurs', 'Conflict entrepreneurs', 'Economic entrepreneurs', 'Marketing entrepreneurs', 'B'),
(250, 'All these are stages in Maslow\'s theory of need except:', 'Self-actualization', 'Self-confidence', 'Safety needs', 'Physiological needs', 'B'),
(251, 'The position of ______ theory is that the reason for any social conflict lies in the social context within which it occurs:', 'Systematic theory', 'Realist theory', 'Biological theory', 'All of the above', 'A'),
(252, 'The position of human needs theory is similar to that of ______:', 'Biological theory', 'Frustration aggression theory', 'Systematic theory', 'Realist theory', 'B'),
(253, '______ is believed to be the biggest source of identity-based conflict:', 'Tribalism', 'Ethnicity', 'Religion', 'Politics', 'B'),
(254, '______ describes life in the \"state of nature\" as solitary, poor, nasty, brutish, and short:', 'Thomas Hobbes', 'Walter Rodney', 'Karl Marx', 'Williams Wilberforce', 'A'),
(255, 'Classical theorists like Thomas Hobbes, St. Augustine, Malthus, and Freud expressed the belief that human beings are driven by a natural instinct to ______:', 'Self-preservation', 'Self-actualization', 'Solidarity', 'Freedom', 'A');
